Thanks!

> A quick question:
>
> I was wondering if the different shading of literal chunks in your RPubs examples (i.e., the dark grey shading down the left side of the block) can be easily implemented – as this is a nice way to highlight the difference between literal chunks and the echoed R code blocks (especially for “beginner” students who might otherwise be confused).  And if it is easy, can the styling be customized, to make the literal chunks even more distinctive.
