> Sometimes you need to save a graphics file for use outside the R/knitr
> ecosystem. Explicit use of ggsave (for example) is proper in these cases.
>
> I do agree that manually saving a plot just to manually insert it in the
> document you are creating is not an efficient way to do things and should
> generally be discouraged. But there are reasons to generate a plot other
> than to just display it in the document being created by knitr.
>
> --Brian Diggs

